        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0601" n="1561" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1561"/>

                <head>No. 1064.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Straus to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 18, 1888</date>.
                        (Received March 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 61.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 49, of
                    December 30, 1887, I have the honor to report that the four closed schools
                    (instead of three, as originally reported to me) of the Board of Foreign
                    Missions of the Reformed Presbyterian Church in Tarsus, Mersine, and Adana, have
                    been re-opened pursuant to the instructions given by the Grand Vizier, and are
                    in full operation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O. S. Straus.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
